# Amendment #65 — D-migration D.4 — pos-new-workspace --from <repo> console-script (β.2 absorbed)

2026-04-26. Fourth of the five D-migration amendments. D.1 (sealed
at 570092a, Amendment #61) restructured canonical pos-v2's
`framework/<component>/` layout. D.1.5 (sealed at 21e27f2,
Amendment #62) added rename-aware seal logic to pos-amend. D.2
(sealed at 7ef1e23, Amendment #63) established the
`<workspace>/workspace/` directory + cut over every reader of
workspace-state paths. D.3 (sealed at 209b6af, Amendment #64)
retired workspace-sync's bespoke pipeline in favour of `git
fetch + git merge --ff-only` against `<workspace>/framework/`.
D.4 closes the new-workspace bootstrap loop: `pos-new-workspace
--from <repo> <new-ws-path>` is a one-verb operator surface that
creates a fresh workspace at the D-shape (framework/ + workspace/
+ .claude/) by cloning canonical + scaffolding workspace-state.

The previously-separate β.2 task (`workspace-sync-ergonomics.md`
§β.2) is **absorbed** into this amendment per the locked D-D4
ruling. β.2's design (separate `pos-new-workspace` console_script,
NOT a `pos` subcommand) is preserved verbatim; the placement
decision (D-β.2 path b.i) lands the entry-point in
`framework/workspace-bootstrap/pyproject.toml` so the module
sits next to the scaffold it composes.

