# Amendment #67 — Single-framework restructure — synthetic framework-only branch + reader fall-through

2026-04-28. The post-D.4 fresh-workspace bootstrap (β.2 absorbed
into D.4 / amendment #65) cloned canonical wholesale into
`<workspace>/framework/`, producing `<workspace>/framework/
framework/<comp>/` (component paths doubled) and
`<workspace>/framework/CLAUDE.md` (top-level docs nested one
level deeper than the four corpus-discovery readers expect). The
pos3 D-shape cutover (commit `938b4c8`) patched it with a fan of
relative symlinks at the workspace root — workspace-specific
cosmetic patch that did NOT survive into future fresh workspaces.

Locked decisions D1–D7 (research §6, pre-attached recommendations,
ruled by Luke at dispatch time):

  - D1: adopt Alternative 4 (subtree-split synthetic branch).
  - D2: NOT Alternative 5 (canonical-side restructure of
    `framework/<comp>/` to `<comp>/`).
  - D3: 4a (reader fall-through), not 4b (bootstrap-time symlinks).
  - D4: custom commit-tree script (~50–100 LOC python) at a NEW
    tools-side home `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/`.
  - D5: probe-and-prefer-workspace-root (handles future workspaces
    with workspace-root-specific overrides).
  - D6: applies on pos3 immediately AND future workspaces (the
    reader fall-through unblocks pos3 simultaneously).
  - D7: branch name `framework-only`.

